      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah, it's always confusing. I'm surprised they never added any tools for users allowing them to know who the owner/master is.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-24T20:18:52.992Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Very simple change currently in the game if you make a world like a private world and have a bunch of people join and eventually more people want to join that world. It doesn't state who the room owner is. So people request and then have to tell the room owner oh hey this person wants in or sometimes doesn't even see the notification. I think it's very beneficial when clicking a player in the social if they are in a friends or private world. It says for example John is in Billy's Private World or (Room Owner is Billy) when clicking on \"John\". Thus removing the awkwardness of having to ask around and figuring out who the room owner is. Instead it will clearly state who owns the room and who to request directly from. Many people room owners aren't my friend but everyone else in the lobby is and it creates conflicts not knowing who is the owner. This will only appear in the social menu not actual in game titles.",
